===============================================================================
SCALE OF ONE TESSELLATION
===============================================================================
  grains per disc                      103.40 +- 3.06
  grain-boundary area                  425.4 +- 7.3 cm^2
  disc volume / boundary area          6.462 mm
  mean distance from a random point
  to the nearest grain boundary        2.614 +- 0.088 mm
  wavelength at 2 MHz, c = 3850 m/s    1.925 mm

  The point-to-boundary figure is the CEILING of the boundary
  offset: two tessellations that know nothing about each other
  put the boundary of one at a typical interior position of the
  other, so no pair can be much farther apart than that. The
  question is how close the pairs come to the ceiling.

