  the f_mis column and its f V / A conversion are the two
  columns microstructure_error.py prints for the same levels,
  recomputed from generators rather than from the raster. Their
  agreement is the check that this module's geometry is that
  module's geometry.

  the two published tolerances, carried into the boundary-
  offset metric by interpolating this curve:
    below 2 of 8 first places at f V/A = 0.420 mm  ->  d_bnd = 0.381 mm
    below 1 of 8 first places at f V/A = 0.575 mm  ->  d_bnd = 0.503 mm

